# What NOT to upload when deploying the API.
#
# Vercel uploads the working directory, not what git tracks, so a .gitignore entry
# does nothing here. `data/backtest-cache` is 19,190 files of local measurement cache
# and on its own it blew the platform's 15,000-file limit:
#
#   Error: Invalid request: `files` should NOT have more than 15000 items, received 19413.
#
# Only `api/` and the part of `src/` it imports actually run in production. Everything
# below is either a local artifact, a test, or the site — which is built and deployed
# by .github/workflows/pages.yml to GitHub Pages, not from here.

# Local caches and stored measurements. The cache is regenerated on demand; the
# results are evidence, kept in git, and of no use to a serverless function.
data/backtest-cache/
data/results/

# Build outputs. The site's is deployed by Pages; the CLI's is built by `prepare`.
dist/
dist-cli/

# Not part of the running API.
test/
docs/
logo/
.github/
*.png
